course: dictionary
lesson: 3089
title: A slippery word: eel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An eel is a long, thin fish that looks like a snake and has slippery skin. Eels have fins and gills, so they live in water. «Electric eels can give a strong shock» tells you this fish has a special power.
explain: When you read about an animal, look for clues in the words around it. «Electric eels breathe air and must gulp at the surface every few minutes» shows that eels are not like every other fish, because they come up for air. Use the clues to picture the eel before you read on.
explain: The phrase «slippery as an eel» is a figure of speech. It does not mean a real fish. It describes someone who is hard to catch or pin down. The rest of the sentence gives you the clue you need.
fact: An eel is a long, thin fish with slippery skin.
fact: Eels have fins and gills, so they live in water.
fact: Some eels travel huge distances to breed.
fact: «Electric eels» can give an electric shock.
fact: «Slippery as an eel» means hard to catch or pin down.
exercise: What is an eel? | A small bird that lives in trees | *A long, thin fish with slippery skin | A kind of snake that lives on land | A type of rock found in rivers
exercise: «Electric eels breathe air and must gulp at the surface every few minutes.» Why must they come up to the surface? | To find food under the rocks | To hide from bigger fish | To keep warm in the sun | *To breathe air
exercise: Mia says, «He is slippery as an eel, you'll never catch him.» What does slippery as an eel mean here? | He likes swimming in rivers | He has wet, slimy skin | *He is hard to catch or pin down | He is a fish
test: «A gulper eel has a mouth so big it can swallow a meal almost its own size.» What can a gulper eel do? | Climb trees | Glow in the dark like a lure | *Swallow a meal almost its own size | Sing to the fish
test: In «Electric eels can leap up and press their chin against a threat», what is a threat? | *Something that could harm the eel | A place to sleep | A type of food | A river bank
exam: «Electric eels send out weak electric pulses to sense things in murky water.» What do the pulses help an eel do? | Fly over the water | Change colour | *Sense things in murky water | Grow new fins
